body: "## Observed CI gap, not a functional regression\n\nAt PR #188 head `2ed0e24c866a2b7c723cda7927ad3765e24e4cef`, the Node 26 job fails the unchanged branch-coverage gate after **537/537 functional tests pass in both the npm and Bun invocations**.\n\nSource job: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-beads/actions/runs/40760622195/job/123071234214\n\nThe Bun invocation reports:\n- aggregate branch coverage **99.96%**, below the required 100%;\n- `index.ts` branch coverage **99.87%**;\n- diagnostic `index.ts:1855 uncovered branch BRDA:1855,518,0,0`.\n\nThe source at that location is the nonzero-exit error fallback:\nhttps://github.com/unbraind/pm-beads/blob/2ed0e24c866a2b7c723cda7927ad3765e24e4cef/index.ts#L1851-L1855\n\n```ts\nif (result.status !== 0) {\n  throw new CommandError(result.stderr || \"pm list failed\");\n}\n```\n\nThe npm invocation passes its gate, Node 22 succeeds, and the new `repair.ts` module is 100% covered. Therefore this report does **not** establish a repair runtime failure, a data-loss defect, or that the new feature introduced the underlying coverage instability. The reason the two invocations cover different branches is not yet established.\n\n## Expected contract and impact\n\nThe canonical feature record explicitly requires the full npm and Bun release gates at unchanged thresholds:\nhttps://github.com/unbraind/pm-beads/blob/2ed0e24c866a2b7c723cda7927ad3765e24e4cef/.agents/pm/features/pm-beads-y6cp.toon\n\nThe current exact-head Node 26 gate is red despite all functional tests passing, blocking the required verification evidence. Keep the 100% threshold rather than lowering it or treating passing test counts as a full gate pass.\n\n## Reproduction/evidence\n\nUse the PR's existing CI sequence on the immutable head above. The npm release check completes; the subsequent Bun release check reaches its coverage phase and fails at the shown branch. Full job logs preserve both invocations and the uncovered-branch diagnostic. This was observed in hosted CI; a complete local Node 26 gate reproduction is not claimed.\n\nIndependent isolated Node 24 checks of the new repair functions passed, but are not evidence that this separate full-gate coverage condition is resolved.\n\n## Acceptance / regression criteria\n\n- Deterministically exercise nonzero `readPmItemsViaSpawn` status with nonempty stderr and with empty stderr, asserting the original stderr and the `pm list failed` fallback respectively.\n- Make the branch coverage independent of incidental child-process warnings or prior invocation state.\n- Re-run exact-head npm and Bun release gates on Node 22 and 26 with the existing 100% thresholds; retain receipts for both invocations.\n- Preserve fail-closed workspace reads and typed command errors. Do not suppress the fallback or weaken the gate merely to pass.\n\nAll-status issue/PR records and the feature record were checked before filing; old #75 is closed general coverage work. This is distinct from daily release publication failures. No provider mutation, published-artifact failure, or deployment claim is made.\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (1)\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-11-02T09:26:18Z)\n>\n> Fixed on main. Evidence: PR #188 merged 2026-10-28 (f45fc81); main CI green incl. Node 22/26 npm+Bun release gates at unchanged thresholds: run 41306885796 (2026-11-01) (Found in the 2026-11-02 triage of issues the blind issue watch missed.)"
